course: dictionary
lesson: 75
title: Across: from one side to the other
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word across tells you where something goes or how far it reaches. It means from one side to the other side. «A girl in Dublin ran across the road to catch the bus» means she crossed from one side of the road to the other.
explain: Across can also mean on the other side, as in «the shop across the road», or it can tell you how wide something is, as in «2 meters across». Read the words around it. Is something moving, sitting in a place, or being measured?
explain: Across can be a preposition or an adverb. In a crossword, across clues run from left to right. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If "from one side to the other" still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Across means from one side to the other side.
fact: «The shop across the road» means the shop on the other side of the road.
fact: «2 meters across» tells you the width, from one side to the other.
fact: «Come across» can mean find by chance, and «across from» means opposite.
fact: «Darwin's bark spider in Madagascar spins webs across rivers up to about 25 metres wide.»
exercise: «A girl in Dublin always ran across the road to catch the bus.» What does across mean here? | Along the middle of the road, with cars | Under the road in a tunnel | *From one side of the road to the other | Very quickly, like a race
exercise: «Darwin's bark spider in Madagascar spins webs across rivers up to about 25 metres wide.» What does across tell us about the webs? | They are cold and wet | They are made of wood | *They reach from one bank of the river to the other | They float on top of the water
exercise: Grandma says, «The shop across the road has the best buns.» What does across mean here? | *On the other side of the road | Inside the road | Under the road | Behind your house
test: «The river is 25 metres across.» What does across tell us? | *The width, from one side to the other | How fast the river flows | How deep the river is | The colour of the river
test: «Each year more than a million wildebeest follow the rain across the Serengeti.» What does across mean here? | Inside a small tent | Up in the sky | Underwater only | *Over a wide area, from one side to the other
exam: Which sentence uses across to mean on the other side? | She ran across the playground. | Sloths can swim across a river. | *The café is across from the school.
